Subject: local: give the sandbox the forge host and an enterprise token placeholder

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. Breadboard-local substitution, recorded under decision 3 of
the Fullsend integration conformance plan. Replaces the upstream-bound
0002-pass-the-forge-host-into-the-sandbox.patch, which upstream made
unsendable.

Inside the sandbox an agent reaches the forge through gh, which takes its
host from GH_HOST and, for any host that is not github.com, its credential
from GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN rather than GH_TOKEN. The old patch passed both
through env.sandbox. Since fullsend-ai/agents#1407 (1271dab) no real forge
token may be expanded into the sandbox: the github-* providers inject an
opaque placeholder and the gateway substitutes the credential on egress to
the profile's endpoints, and scripts/sandbox-credential-boundary-test.sh
enforces it. Passing GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN through env.sandbox would put the
real minted token back in the sandbox.

So the token half moves into the provider. The github-code provider declares
GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN as a second credential carrying the same minted token,
and the fullsend-github-code profile accepts it as a stored key (OpenShell
0.1.x rejects a provider credential its profile does not declare). The
sandbox therefore sees a second placeholder, never the token. Only GH_HOST,
which is not a secret, goes through env.sandbox, in the GitHub block of every
harness that has one: triage, review, code, fix, prioritize and retro.
Scribe has no GitHub sandbox access and is untouched.

The github-ro provider, which triage, review, prioritize and retro use, is
embedded in the fullsend binary; its half of this change is in fullsend
patch 0016.

On github.com GH_HOST expands empty, which gh treats as unset.

Breadboard note: applied to the agents mirror by
deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py.

